From b8cf665fb4decda8e684a725103c99068cbf97d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 21:07:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-88: outline Ctrl+H / Ctrl+L, zoom 12.5-800 %,
 artboard background, like WPF (0.88.0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

WPF XAML Designer (Create UIs > Document Outline): "press Ctrl+H to hide an
element and Shift+Ctrl+H to show it", "Ctrl+L to lock ... Shift+Ctrl+L to
unlock". Now ht9045Designer.designKey (hide / show / lock / unlock) works on
the design surface's selection (every selected one) or, from the component
tree, on the tree's selected rows; the surface's keys are not bound while the
tree has the focus, and neither is the surface's F2 any more (in the tree F2
renamed the surface's selection, not the row).

Zoom (Create UIs > artboard toolbar): "You can zoom from 12.5% to 800%". The
steps now go 12.5 % .. 800 % (list, + / -, Ctrl+wheel); fit and fit selection
still pick at most 400 %; the label says 12.5 %.

"Toggle artboard background: Toggles between a light and dark background": a
背景 button on the toolbar -- the page's own background or a dark one (inline
on html / body, the page's own values put back), for every page, remembered,
the page as it is in the operate mode.

WPF_DIFF_LOG.md: items 11-13 done (0.87 commit filled in).

Tests (all 4 layers pass: lib 159, smoke 178, panels, real VS Code 153):
smoke (surface spbSave + sbtExit hidden / shown, tree Panel2 + sbtExit locked /
unlocked, the key rules apart, the artboard setting kept); probe (both zoom
ends, + stops at 800 %, 12.5 % label, clamped; the background dark and back);
real VS Code (Ctrl+H / Shift+Ctrl+H on spbSave, the source untouched).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
